WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Praise the Lord! In more than forty years of marriage, we have experienced many testimonies of God.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Each experience has shown us that God is trustworthy.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Near the end of his life, Paul said, “I know whom I have believed.”

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Brothers and sisters, do not fear the process. We live in the microwave age, but life cannot mature in thirty seconds.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Growth in life takes time. We experience the Lord each day in our ordinary lives.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:01:03.000
In Exodus, the tenth plague brought darkness over Egypt—darkness so deep that people could not see one another.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Pharaoh summoned Moses, but still would not let the people go.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:27.000
Pharaoh said, “Get away from me! The day you see my face again, you will die.”

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:40.000
If this had been Moses’ first time before Pharaoh, he might have been afraid to return.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:51.000
But after one experience after another, Moses knew that God was far greater than Pharaoh.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:02:01.000
At first Moses asked, “Who am I?” God answered, “I will be with you.”

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:18.000
God’s presence was what mattered. Pharaoh threatened to kill him if he returned, and Moses answered, “I will not see you again either.”

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:31.000
Brothers and sisters, do not fear difficult circumstances; they can help us know God more.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:45.000
Paul says in 2 Timothy, “I know whom I have believed.”

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:56.000
Pharaoh once said, “Who is Jehovah? I do not know Him.” But through the whole process, Moses came to know Jehovah.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.000
He was also convinced that God could guard what he had entrusted to Him.
